(2268878, 309632, 11897, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by stdavidson:</b></div><hr/><i> This makes a good study in low-key still life imagery. I like the tones and lighting angle. There is a slight bit of haloing around the pollen and the leftmost petal lacks detail, but this is basic rules and you cannot do much about it. I recommend you correct those should you chose to make a print. Great picture that should place very high. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Steve,<br/>I agree with your comments totally, altered it for print very slightly.<br/> <br/>Paul.</td>', 'Originally posted by stdavidson: This makes a good study in low-key still life imagery. I like the tones and lighting angle. There is a slight bit of haloing around the pollen and the leftmost petal lacks detail, but this is basic rules and you cannot do much about it. I recommend you correct those should you chose to make a print. Great picture that should place very high.   Thanks Steve,I agree with your comments totally, altered it for print very slightly. Paul.', '2006-03-29 04:21:14.000000', NULL, 0),
